<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net10.0;net8.0;net9.0;netstandard2.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<RootNamespace>DevOp.Toon</RootNamespace>
		<AssemblyName>DevOp.Toon</AssemblyName>

		<!-- Package Information -->
		<PackageId>DevOp.Toon</PackageId>
		<Version>0.4.0</Version>
		<Authors>Þorvaldur Hafdal</Authors>
		<Company>DevOp</Company>
		<Description>Token-Oriented Object Notation (TOON) - a token-efficient JSON alternative for LLM prompts</Description>
		<PackageTags>toon;format;llm;token;serialization;json</PackageTags>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.md</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://wiki.devop.is/devop-toon/home</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/vhafdal/DevOp.Toon</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<SignAssembly>true</SignAssembly>
		<AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>DevOp.snk</AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>
		<PublicSign>true</PublicSign>
		<Title>DevOp Toon</Title>
		<Copyright>Þorvaldur Hafdal(DevOp)</Copyright>
		<PackageIcon>Assets\DevOp.Toon-128.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>Adds opt-in constant columns for custom 4.4 tables and [ToonExtensionData] support on the legacy profiles, and fixes legacy encoding and typed decoding gaps.
- Adds ToonEncodeOptions.ConstantColumns (default false): with CustomV4_4, a column identical in every row of a table with at least three rows is written once in the header as Name=value, which CustomV4_4 decoding applies to every row; readers from 0.4.0 and earlier cannot decode it; Auto detection now selects CustomV4_4 for an unquoted '=' in a header field list, so such hand-written official input needs an explicit ProtocolVersion
- Breaking: V3_0 and CustomLegacy now write [ToonExtensionData] entries as sibling keys and capture unmatched keys on typed decode, like the 4.x profiles; a key named like the extension property is an ordinary entry, so a 0.4.0 legacy document with the property as a nested object now decodes as a single entry named after the property
- Breaking: keys that name a declared but unbindable member, such as a computed getter-only property, are no longer captured into [ToonExtensionData] on 4.x profiles
- Adds capture of unmatched keys to ToonService.Deserialize&lt;T&gt;(body, "application/json") with numbers as double, while decimal members now receive the exact JSON value; a JSON number beyond the double range, or beyond the decimal range of a decimal member, now throws ToonFormatException instead of yielding an infinity or an OverflowException
- Fixes V3_0 and CustomLegacy encoding: root and declared dictionaries are written as objects, as are types implementing only the generic dictionary interfaces (such as ExpandoObject) on every protocol version; byte arrays inside lists of objects follow ByteArrayFormat; key folding also folds chains below the root; IgnoreNullOrEmpty also omits null, empty and non-finite members of nested objects; scalars in object-typed members of rows are written as columns
- Fixes V3_0 and CustomLegacy typed decoding of structs and of struct dictionary and list members, of int and long members on the path-expansion route, of nested objects in Dictionary&lt;string, object?&gt; targets, of settable members of records outside the constructor, and of list items whose first field is an array, which no longer lose decimal digits; a number outside the range of a numeric member now throws ToonFormatException on every route, including JSON Deserialize, instead of decoding as 0 or an infinity or failing with NotSupportedException; a fraction into an integer member throws ToonFormatException as on 4.x, and other tokens in numeric members on the direct route decode or fail as on 4.x
- Fixes encoding of System.Text.Json JsonNode values (JsonObject, JsonArray, JsonValue), which overflowed the stack; they now encode like their JSON text on every protocol version, at the root and as members, list items and dictionary values, and V3_0 and CustomLegacy no longer write a blank line for a member that IgnoreNullOrEmpty or ExcludeEmptyArrays omits
- Breaking: typed 4.x decoding throws ToonFormatException (kind Syntax, with the line of the token) instead of OverflowException, FormatException, ArgumentException or InvalidCastException when a token does not fit a numeric, enum, bool, Guid, char, date, time, Uri, Version or byte array member, on every shape; float and double members no longer receive an infinity or NaN, from a number beyond their range or from text such as Infinity or NaN, on 4.x and on the V3_0 and CustomLegacy direct route
- Breaking: on typed decode a number with a fractional part no longer rounds half to even into a byte, sbyte, short or ushort member or an enum member on any of them; it throws ToonFormatException, as it now also does for int, uint, long and ulong members, which threw OverflowException; integral forms such as 1e3, 2.0 and -0.0 still bind (-0.0 now also into uint and ulong), float members are read from the text with a single rounding, decimal members keep the scale of the text on every shape, and on V3_0 and CustomLegacy float and double members receive -0 as 0, as on 4.x
- Fixes typed decoding on 4.x profiles of an unquoted number or true/false into a string member, which became a double rendering (9007199254740993 became 9007199254740992, 1.50 became 1.5) or True/False, and now keeps the token text; and on the V3_0 and CustomLegacy direct route of enum, bool, Guid, char, date and time members, which kept their default or threw NotSupportedException for a token they could not parse (or wrapped an out-of-range enum number) and now bind or throw ToonFormatException as on 4.x
- Fixes V3_0 and CustomLegacy typed decoding: SortedDictionary&lt;string, T&gt;, Dictionary&lt;string, T&gt; subclasses and other string-keyed dictionaries with a parameterless constructor and the non-generic IDictionary now receive their entries instead of decoding empty, and a subclass receives only entries, not its own properties; types that contain themselves through a list, dictionary or member, such as tree nodes, now decode those members instead of losing them; with ExpandPaths Safe, dotted keys below the root, such as the nested chains key folding writes, now expand at every depth and inside arrays instead of decoding as null, and a quoted dotted key, array key or tabular field stays literal; with ExpandPaths Off, a target with a byte array member no longer expands dotted root keys; on the path-expansion route and JSON Deserialize, null, true/false and text in numeric and enum members bind as on 4.x (null as 0, true as 1, "42" as 42, 007 into an enum as 7) or throw ToonFormatException, instead of failing with NotSupportedException; and ToonService with a pinned decode ProtocolVersion, strict decoding and the default decode indent now reads its own output when the encode indent is not a multiple of 2, such as the default indent 1
- Breaking: V3_0 and CustomLegacy typed decoding of a root target or member throws NotSupportedException when a value arrives for a dictionary type it cannot key or construct, where 0.4.0 decoded it as an empty dictionary: dictionaries with non-string keys (int, Guid, enum), Hashtable, the non-generic OrderedDictionary, types implementing only IDictionary&lt;string, T&gt; such as ExpandoObject, and classes implementing only IReadOnlyDictionary; an empty dictionary is a value too, so a non-null empty Dictionary&lt;int, T&gt; member, which V3_0 writes as V:, or a JSON {} now throws; an absent or null member still decodes, as on 4.x
- Breaking: with ExpandPaths Safe on V3_0 and CustomLegacy, unquoted dotted keys below the root now expand into nested objects, including dictionary keys such as Hosts: { "example.com": 1 }, which the encoder writes unquoted and has no option to quote, so they decode as Hosts.example.com; leave ExpandPaths Off for such data</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>true</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="LICENSE.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="Assets\DevOp.Toon-128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="Assets\" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<Using Include="DevOp.Toon.Core" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="DevOp.Toon.Core" Version="0.3.0" Condition="'$(Configuration)' != 'Debug' or '$(ToonCoreProjectPath)' == ''" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Debug' and '$(ToonCoreProjectPath)' != ''">
		<ProjectReference Include="$(ToonCoreProjectPath)" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition=" '$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' ">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Collections.Immutable" Version="10.0.2" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' ">
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
	</PropertyGroup>


</Project>
